      "id": "kheyks1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Banking"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) serves as the central bank and chief regulatory body of the Indian banking structure.",
        "Commercial banks in India are broadly divided into Scheduled Commercial Banks and Non-Scheduled Banks under the RBI Act, 1934.",
        "Primary functions of RBI include issuing currency, managing monetary policy, controlling credit, and acting as banker to the government.",
        "Standard bank account types include Savings Account, Current Account, Fixed Deposit (FD), and Recurring Deposit (RD).",
        "Monetary policy tools are divided into quantitative tools (CRR, SLR, Repo Rate, Bank Rate) and qualitative tools.",
        "Modern digital banking services include real-time and batch settlement systems like UPI, NEFT, RTGS, and IMPS."
      ],
      "id": "h1l3iov"
    },
