      "content": "7. Modern Banking Services"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "seulm55"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "RBI was established on April 1, 1935 under the Reserve Bank of India Act, 1934, and nationalized on January 1, 1949.",
        "Repo Rate is the rate at which RBI lends money to commercial banks, whereas Reverse Repo Rate is the rate at which RBI absorbs liquidity from banks.",
        "Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR) requires banks to hold a specified percentage of Net Demand and Time Liabilities (NDTL) as cash reserves with the RBI.",
        "RTGS (Real Time Gross Settlement) requires a minimum transfer amount of ₹2 Lakhs, whereas NEFT has no minimum transfer limit."
      ],
      "id": "hdafwyb"
